   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Every floor has to send",
    "its weight somewhere.",
    "So which beams",
    "actually feel this cat?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 6.1,
   "chunks": [
    "The piece of floor",
    "each beam carries",
    "is called its TRIBUTARY AREA."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 11.0,
   "chunks": [
    "First, check the panel's shape.",
    "Divide the long side",
    "by the short side."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 16.0,
   "chunks": [
    "18 by 6 is a ratio of 3.",
    "More than 2",
    "means a ONE-WAY slab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 21.8,
   "chunks": [
    "The load runs straight across",
    "to the two long beams.",
    "Each one carries",
    "half the short span:",
    "a uniform load."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 29.9,
   "chunks": [
    "Now squish it closer to square.",
    "12 by 9 is about 1.3.",
    "2 or less",
    "means TWO-WAY."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 37.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Draw 45\u00b0 lines",
    "from every corner.",
    "Now the load flows",
    "to all four edges."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 44.2,
   "chunks": [
    "The short beams get triangles.",
    "The long beams get trapezoids."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 49.3,
   "chunks": [
    "Same floor,",
    "same load per square foot.",
    "Just a different shape,",
    "and a different load path."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 55.3,
   "chunks": [
    "Long and skinny: one way.",
    "Close to square: two ways."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 59.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Follow for the next teardown."
   ]
  }
